Package: com.qingc12.pullovermf
Name: PullOverMF
Version: 0.1.4
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: MultiFloat personal fork of PullOver X (GPL-3.0). Floating multitask window / split view for iOS 14+ (roothide / arm64e). 0.1.4: CRITICAL LINK FIX - 0.1.2 and 0.1.3 both failed to load entirely (no handle, no log file at all) because PullOverX.mm is ObjC++ and called cross-file C functions that were declared WITHOUT extern "C": the compiler emitted C++-mangled references (__Z9MFLogRawCPKc, __Z19MFRingPickerInstallv) while the definitions export plain C names (_MFLogRawC, _MFRingPickerInstall), so dyld could not resolve them and rejected the whole dylib. The prefix header now wraps every shared C interface in extern "C". 0.1.3 content: Stheno-style ring picker - a semicircular dial pinned to the screen edge with app icons along the arc (modelled on Stheno's RingView/RingType), tap an icon to pin that app and open the float, long-press to remove it (persisted to ringApps), summoned by a configurable edge-gesture strip; plus pure-C MFLogRawC() logging to /var/mobile/PullOverMF.log for the constructor phase.
Maintainer: QingC12
Author: PullOver X by mlgm / PullOver Pro by c1d3rDev / fork by QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 14.0)
Priority: optional
